            <ArticleTitle>Mydriasis due to self-administered inhaled ipratropium bromide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>178</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mydriasis due to ipratropium bromide has previously been described in children and adults. Children as young as 4 years of age may attempt to self-administer their inhalers. This possibility should be considered if an asthmatic child presents with abnormal neurological signs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
